    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Founded by the commoner <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#liu-bang">Liu Bang</a> in 202 BCE, the Han replaced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#qin-dynasty">Qin</a> brutality with Confucian government and lasted four centuries.</li><li>It opened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#silk-road">Silk Road</a>, drove back the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu</a> and built a bureaucratic model of rule that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#china">China</a> kept until 1912.</li><li>Landed elites, court feuds and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#yellow-turban-rebellion">Yellow Turban Rebellion</a> handed power to warlords, and the dynasty ended in 220.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#china">China</a>'s majority ethnic group still calls itself Han, after this dynasty, more than eighteen centuries after it fell.</p></aside>
    </section>

